 # Spherical Beta View-Dependent Color
 
-Also called: Beta Splatting, Spherical Beta (SB) appearance model, Spherical Beta lobes
+Also called: Spherical Beta, Spherical Beta (SB) appearance model, Spherical Beta lobes
 
 ## Overview
-Spherical Beta (SB) is a specular appearance model that adds explicit specular lobes on top of a diffuse base color, used for view-dependent color in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. It is distinct from Spherical Harmonics (SH) by using a parametric lobe function rather than a global basis expansion, allowing for sharper highlights with fewer parameters [S2, unofficial]. It is orthogonal to SH, where SH (typically degree 0) supplies the diffuse base and SB adds the specular component [S3, unofficial].
+Spherical Beta (SB) is a specular appearance model that adds explicit specular lobes on top of a diffuse base color for view-dependent rendering in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1, unofficial]. It replaces higher SH bands with parametric lobes, achieving sharper highlights with fewer parameters while remaining orthogonal to the SH diffuse base [S2, S3, unofficial].
 
